{
  "id": "m35l1",
  "title": {
    "es": "Técnicas con diccionarios",
    "en": "Dictionary techniques"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Más allá de clave/valor"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`dict.get(clave, defecto)` evita errores si la clave no existe. Es la base para contar cosas sin comprobar antes si la clave está."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "cuenta = {}",
          "for ch in 'banana':",
          "    cuenta[ch] = cuenta.get(ch, 0) + 1",
          "print(cuenta)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "{'b': 1, 'a': 3, 'n': 2}"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`.items()` recorre pares (clave, valor); `.keys()` y `.values()` dan claves y valores."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Para invertir un dict, recuerda que las claves deben ser únicas (si hay valores repetidos, perderás alguno)."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Beyond key/value"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`dict.get(key, default)` avoids errors if the key is missing. It's the basis for counting things without checking first."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "cuenta = {}",
          "for ch in 'banana':",
          "    cuenta[ch] = cuenta.get(ch, 0) + 1",
          "print(cuenta)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "{'b': 1, 'a': 3, 'n': 2}"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`.items()` iterates (key, value) pairs; `.keys()` and `.values()` give keys and values."
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "To invert a dict, remember keys must be unique (with repeated values you'll lose some)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m35l1e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `contar_letras(texto)` que devuelva un dict letra -> nº de apariciones (usa get).",
        "en": "Define `contar_letras(texto)` returning a dict letter -> count (use get)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def contar_letras(texto):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def contar_letras(texto):",
        "    cuenta = {}",
        "    for ch in texto:",
        "        cuenta[ch] = cuenta.get(ch, 0) + 1",
        "    return cuenta"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "cuenta[ch] = cuenta.get(ch, 0) + 1."
        ],
        "en": [
          "cuenta[ch] = cuenta.get(ch, 0) + 1."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "contar_letras",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "aab"
              ],
              "expected": {
                "a": 2,
                "b": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "args": [
                ""
              ],
              "expected": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m35l1e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `invertir(d)` que intercambie claves y valores (todos cadenas).",
        "en": "Define `invertir(d)` swapping keys and values (all strings)."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def invertir(d):",
        "    pass"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def invertir(d):",
        "    return {v: k for k, v in d.items()}"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Comprensión de dict: {v: k for k, v in d.items()}."
        ],
        "en": [
          "Dict comprehension: {v: k for k, v in d.items()}."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "function": "invertir",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                {
                  "a": "x",
                  "b": "y"
                }
              ],
              "expected": {
                "x": "a",
                "y": "b"
              }
            },
            {
              "args": [
                {}
              ],
              "expected": {}
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}